# Scenario 1: Collect the friends (part 1: Maja picks up Even)
# {{maja}} etc. are the names the players typed in at the start.
# Inventory.has("id"), Inventory.give("id"), Inventory.take("id") work with items.
# flag("x") / set_flag("x") remember things during the scenario.

~ intro
{{maja}}: Finally! A whole week in a cabin in the mountains. No city, no traffic, no work.
{{maja}}: First I pick up {{even}}, then {{sara}} and {{tom}}.
{{maja}}: ...but I need my car keys. I lent the spare set to Mrs. Berg next door.
=> END

~ car
if Inventory.has("car_keys") and flag("even_joined")
	{{maja}}: Keys, check. {{even}}, check. Let's go!
	=> drive_off
elif Inventory.has("car_keys")
	{{maja}}: I've got the keys, but I'm not leaving without {{even}}. He lives in the blue building across the road.
else
	{{maja}}: Locked. Mrs. Berg still has my keys.
=> END

~ drive_off
{{even}}: Hey, I just looked at the booking for the cabin. It says "cabin for 5 guests".
{{maja}}: Five? There are only four of us.
{{even}}: So who is number five?
{{maja}}: ...Probably a typo. Seatbelts on!
$> finish()
=> END

~ berg
if Inventory.has("car_keys")
	Mrs. Berg: Drive safely, dear! And bring warm socks, the mountains are cold.
	=> END
if Inventory.has("post")
	Mrs. Berg: Oh, my post! You're an angel.
	$> Inventory.take("post")
	Mrs. Berg: Now, your keys... here you are.
	$> Inventory.give("car_keys")
	Mrs. Berg: Funny thing. There was a postcard with a picture of a mountain cabin.
	Mrs. Berg: It's addressed to "the fifth guest". No name. Is that for you?
	- That's odd. What does it say?
		Mrs. Berg: Just "See you up there. Save me a beer." And it smells of cigarettes.
		{{maja}}: ...Weird.
	- Not ours. Must be for another house.
		Mrs. Berg: Hm. I'll keep it on the fridge, then.
	$> set_flag("saw_postcard")
	=> END
Mrs. Berg: Hello, dear! Off on your big trip?
- Yes! Do you still have my car keys?
	Mrs. Berg: Of course. But my knees are bad today. Could you fetch my post from the mailbox by the road first?
	{{maja}}: Sure, back in a minute.
	$> set_flag("asked_for_post")
- Just saying hi!
	Mrs. Berg: Hello, hello! Don't forget your keys, dear.
=> END

~ mailbox
if Inventory.has("post") or Inventory.has("car_keys")
	{{maja}}: Empty now.
elif flag("asked_for_post")
	{{maja}}: Mrs. Berg's post. Some letters and a postcard.
	$> Inventory.give("post")
else
	{{maja}}: Mrs. Berg's mailbox. Not mine to open.
=> END

~ even
if flag("even_joined")
	{{even}}: Coming, coming!
	=> END
{{even}}: {{maja}}! I'm almost ready. I just need to answer a few work emails first.
{{even}}: Forty. Maybe a hundred.
{{maja}}: You promised. No work this week.
=> even_choice

~ even_choice
{{even}}: But what if something breaks while I'm away?
- Your team will survive one week without you.
	{{even}}: Will they, though?
	{{maja}}: Yes. And your doctor told you to rest.
	=> even_choice
- Set an out-of-office reply. Right now.
	{{even}}: "Out of office until next week. Please don't call." ...Send. Wow. That felt good.
	$> set_flag("even_out_of_office")
	=> even_leaves
- Give me the laptop. It stays here.
	{{even}}: My laptop? Fine. FINE. But I'm keeping my phone.
	$> set_flag("even_left_laptop")
	=> even_leaves

~ even_leaves
{{even}}: Okay. To the cabin! I'll wait in the car.
$> even_joins()
=> END
